{
  "id": "functional-plateau",
  "term": "functional plateau",
  "definition": "In diabetic macular edema, functional plateau means that the retinal swelling has settled or cleared, but vision remains poor or stops improving. It describes a mismatch in which anatomical improvement occurs without further functional recovery.",
